nce to a period of 104 weeks. (8) The applicant is not entitled to the disability premium if he has, or is treated as having, limited capability for work.

Severe disability premium 11.—(1) The condition is that the applicant is a severely disabled person. (2) For the purposes of sub-paragraph (1), an applicant is to be treated as being a severely disabled person if, and only if— (a) in the case of a single applicant, a lone parent or an applicant who is treated as having no partner in consequence of sub-paragraph (3)— (i) he is in receipt of— (aa) attendance allowance; (aaa) pension age disability payment;

