Calculation of weekly income 17.—(1) Except in a case within sub-paragraph (2), (3A), (4A) or (5), for the purposes of calculating the weekly income of an applicant, where the period in respect of which payment is made— (a) does not exceed a week, the whole of that payment must be included in the applicant’s weekly income; (b) exceeds a week, the amount to be included in the applicant’s weekly income is to be determined— (i) in a case where that period is a month, by multiplying the amount of the payment by 12 and dividing the product by 52; (ii) in a case where that period is three months, by multiplying the amount of the payment by 4 and dividing the product by 52;

